# Option B Launch Features: Walkthrough & Verification

This walkthrough summarizes the changes made to implement passenger reporting, offline caching, and web push notifications, and presents the verification outputs.

---

## 🛠️ Changes Implemented

### 1. Database & Mock Storage
* **[schema.sql](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/db/schema.sql)**: Added table schemas for `passenger_reports` (storing delay types, descriptions, and GPS locations) and `push_subscriptions` (storing browser endpoints and auth keys).
* **[index.ts (DB)](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/db/index.ts)**: Extended the local mock database queries to intercept reports and subscriptions, allowing full local simulation and testing without a live PostgreSQL instance.

### 2. Backend API & Ingestion
* **[notificationService.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/services/notificationService.ts) [NEW]**: Configured `web-push` to manage public/private VAPID credentials (with auto-generation on session start if missing from `.env`), save subscriptions, and push alerts.
* **[index.ts (App)](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/index.ts)**:
  * Implemented REST endpoints for submitting reports (`POST /api/v1/reports`), fetching active reports (`GET /api/v1/reports/active`), retrieving the VAPID key (`GET /api/v1/push/key`), subscribing (`POST /api/v1/push/subscribe`), and unsubscribing (`POST /api/v1/push/unsubscribe`).
* **[stopStateFSM.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/engine/stopStateFSM.ts)**: Configured stop-state transitions (`arriving_now` and `on_stop`) to trigger push alerts automatically when a bus enters a stop geofence.
* **[eta.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/engine/eta.ts)**: Updated the FSM updating payload in the ETA engine to supply stop names so push alerts have descriptive stops info.

### 3. Frontend Service Worker & Caching
* **[sw.js](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/web-app/public/sw.js) [NEW]**: Built a service worker that:
  * Caches static app shell resources.
  * Caches dynamic stops endpoints (`/api/v1/routes/:id/stops` and `/api/v1/search/*`) using a network-first strategy for offline lookup.
  * Listens to the `push` event to trigger native system-level notifications.
* **[swHelper.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/web-app/src/app/utils/swHelper.ts) [NEW]**: Added helper utilities to handle client-side worker registration, request notification permissions, and register/deregister VAPID subscriptions.

### 4. Frontend UI & Live Map
* **[LiveMap.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/web-app/src/app/components/LiveMap.tsx)**: Updated Leaflet configurations to accept an array of passenger reports and display them as warning markers on the map, with custom click popups based on report type.
* **[page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/web-app/src/app/page.tsx)**:
  * Registered the service worker on mount.
  * Added active report polling (every 10 seconds) to feed the maps.
  * Added **Notify Me** button which subscribes the user to notifications when tracking a bus.
  * Added **Report Status** button rendering a modal form where passengers can log delays or overcrowding.

