## 📋 Engineering PRD Audit & Alignment

We conducted a thorough audit of the project against the "MY BUS — Engineering PRD" requirements and implemented the missing components and alignments:

### 1. Divergence Nodes Configuration & Ingestion
* **[data.json](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/db/data.json)**: Seeded the `divergence_nodes` configuration with Phandpuri Junction (lat: 29.93, lng: 77.45) and defined its two split branches pointing to Nakur (`routeIds: [9, 12]`) and Ambehta (`routeIds: [200, 201, 246]`).
* **[divergenceBinding.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/engine/divergenceBinding.ts)**: Exported the loaded `divergenceCache` list so it can be dynamically queried.
* **[eta.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/engine/eta.ts)**: Integrated the divergence branch matching algorithm into the live route resolver. If a bus approaches the junction, its coordinates now override the generic text-description route association, matching it to the correct active path.

### 2. Intermediate Village Corridor Filtering (150m-200m)
* **[routeVillages.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/api/routeVillages.ts)**: Restructured the cache-saving logic to maintain the full 5 km candidate dataset on disk, while default searches filter and return only the intermediate villages situated within a tight 200m (0.2 km) corridor of the route line as specified in Section 1.3 of the PRD.

### 3. Alternative Routing Card & Geofence Tunings
* **[page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/web-app/src/app/page.tsx)**: Implemented Alternative Routing Card Integration in the frontend routes list, displaying the active bus registration badge (e.g. `[UP 11 FT 4321]`) next to the route's distance indicator if a bus is running on the variant branch.
* **[stopStateFSM.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/engine/stopStateFSM.ts)**: Updated FSM geofencing constants to match the PRD's 50m geofence requirements (`ON_STOP_RADIUS_KM = 0.05` and `ON_STOP_EXIT_RADIUS_KM = 0.10`).

### 4. Route Matching Bugfix (Console Error Resolution)
* **[divergenceBinding.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/engine/divergenceBinding.ts)**: Fixed the runtime `TypeError` (`pointToPolylineDistKm is not a function`) by importing and using the correct `distanceToPolylineKm` function with formatted `Coordinate` objects.
* **[eta.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/engine/eta.ts)** & **[page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/web-app/src/app/page.tsx)**: Exposed the resolved `routeId` from the backend's live tracking details, and updated the frontend `handleTrackBus` to query villages using this `routeId` directly. This resolves the `No route matched for routeCode` console warning.

### 5. Timeline & Map Route Truncation to Search Bounds
* **[page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/web-app/src/app/page.tsx)**: Restructured the live tracking render block to dynamically slice the stops array based on the user's `from` and `to` search queries. When a passenger tracks a bus for a sub-route (e.g. Saharanpur to Phandpuri), the Stops & Live Progress timeline and map polyline are truncated at the user's destination (Phandpuri) instead of drawing all the way to the route end depot (Gangoh).

### 6. Leaflet Map Invalidation Race Condition Bugfix
* **[LiveMap.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/web-app/src/app/components/LiveMap.tsx)**: Fixed the unhandled exception `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading '_leaflet_pos')` by storing the `setTimeout` reference during map container size invalidation (`map.invalidateSize()`) and properly clearing it via `clearTimeout` in the `useEffect` cleanup return block.

